Optimal Solution - Use Dijkstra’s algorithm with asymmetric edge costs to find the minimum cost path.
                    i model the problem as a weighted graph with asymmetric edges and apply Dijkstra to compute the shortest path.

class Solution {
    // Pair class to store (node, distance)
    static class Pair {
        int node;
        int dist;
        Pair(int node, int dist) {
            this.node = node;
            this.dist = dist;
        }
    }
    public int minCost(int n, int[][] edges) {
        // Adjacency list:
        // u -> (v, wt)
        // v -> (u, 2 * wt)  [reverse edge with double cost]
        Map<Integer, List<Pair>> adj = new HashMap<>();
        // Build the graph
        for (int[] edge : edges) {
            int u = edge[0];
            int v = edge[1];
            int wt = edge[2];
            // Forward edge
            adj.computeIfAbsent(u, k -> new ArrayList<>())
               .add(new Pair(v, wt));
            // Reverse edge with double weight
            adj.computeIfAbsent(v, k -> new ArrayList<>())
               .add(new Pair(u, 2 * wt));
        }
        // Distance array initialized to infinity
        int[] dist = new int[n];
        Arrays.fill(dist, Integer.MAX_VALUE);
        // Distance to source node (0) is 0
        dist[0] = 0;
        // Min-heap priority queue (Dijkstra)
        PriorityQueue<Pair> pq =
                new PriorityQueue<>((a, b) -> a.dist - b.dist);
        // Start from node 0
        pq.offer(new Pair(0, 0));
        // Dijkstra's algorithm
        while (!pq.isEmpty()) {
            Pair cur = pq.poll();
            int node = cur.node;
            int d = cur.dist;
            // Skip outdated (stale) entries
            if (d > dist[node])
                continue;
            // If destination reached, return shortest distance
            if (node == n - 1)
                return d;
            // If node has no outgoing edges
            if (!adj.containsKey(node))
                continue;
            // Relax edges
            for (Pair nei : adj.get(node)) {
                int nextNode = nei.node;
                int weight = nei.dist;
                if (d + weight < dist[nextNode]) {
                    dist[nextNode] = d + weight;
                    pq.offer(new Pair(nextNode, dist[nextNode]));
                }
            }
        }
        // Destination unreachable
        return -1;
    }
}

Time Complexity :- O((V + E) log V).
Space Complexity :- O(V + E).
